# Same bytes on Windows and Linux: text stays LF everywhere (shell scripts break with CRLF, libsync compares bytes),
# Windows batch/PowerShell files are CRLF, game/binary files are never converted.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vmap binary
*.vpk binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.radgen binary
